                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2202,
                    "udi": "umb://media/f91ea381a41c4e50be1b200c2e2da210",
                    "image": "/media/q4rb34i2/otms-11.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2200,
                    "udi": "umb://media/ca298eac95564387ae73422019277135",
                    "image": "/media/vkhctssw/otms-16.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            },
            {
              "grid": "6",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p><strong>Tell us about your time with Roadlab. <br /></strong></p>\n<p>I started at Roadlab on December 1<sup>st</sup> 2015, right out of matric. I began in our Germiston facility as an assistant materials tester in the concrete lab.</p>\n<p>I didn’t have a strong idea of what I really wanted to do with my life but I learnt very quickly and began to develop a passion for the industry. After about 6 months I became a technician.</p>\n<p>I spent the next 2 years driving from quarry to quarry, picking up samples, performing densities and making of cubes before ending up on a site lab with Jaques Steyn, Roadlab’s concrete technologist.</p>\n<p>I began my studies of concrete technology while absorbing all the information I could from him.</p>\n<p>I eventually returned to our Germiston facility as the concrete lab manager. I was in that role for 2 years before moving into the role of Group Business Development Manager.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "<p><strong>You were assistant manager on the site lab that was responsible for ensuring the quality, workability and strength of 800 cubic meters of concrete cast each day on the Oiltanking MOGS Saldanha project.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What was that like?<br /></strong></p>\n<p>Our Operations Director Nico Herbst though it would be a great idea for me to be put onto a site lab to get hands-on experience on a construction site.</p>\n<p>It was an opportunity to go work on the biggest construction project in the country at the time, and it was a very humbling experience being able to work on a site of this magnitude at such a young age.</p>\n<p>It taught me an immense amount.</p>\n<p>The OTMS project I believe actually kicked off my career as I got my first opportunity to be an assistant site lab manager.</p>\n<p>By the end of the project I was the Site Lab Manager.</p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        },
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "1c809c1c-1d5e-42e7-8a97-f935b015b33d",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p> </p>\n<p><strong>The PnP Eastport distribution centre just set a world record for the longest roof span covered by a single corrugated sheet. What has it been like being involved in that project?</strong></p>\n<p>It's great to see that we have experts in the industry who are able to pull of a job of this size in such a short time period while ensuring that quality of work is still outstanding and setting a world record.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>You’ve been developing Roadlab’s capacity for testing shotcrete at some of South Africa’s largest mines. What has that been like?<br /></strong></p>\n<p>Shotcrete testing is a new development that I would like to one day have as a standard offering within our group. But it has not been solely me that is working towards this goal.</p>\n<p>It takes a lot of research and training to provide these new testing capabilities, as we need to ensure the same quality of work our clients expect from our standard offering.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2204,
                    "udi": "umb://media/c411f510da594e93a649bc26b5647429",
                    "image": "/media/c10bdrcz/venetia-3.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "<p><em>Roadlab will soon begin testing shotcrete at the Venetia Underground Project. It remains the largest investment spend for both De Beers Group and Anglo American in South Africa and will extend the life-of-mine to 2046.</em></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>What misunderstandings about material testing and quality assurance do you encounter in the industry?</strong></p>\n<p>One of the most common misunderstandings is the actual process and timing of different testing methods.</p>\n<p>Some tests produce results immediately, like nuclear densities and GPR scanning. Others might take months to yield a result, like soil or concrete mix designs.</p>\n<p>Some work requires more regular testing, like nuclear density testing for roadworks or concrete sampling and DCP testing for deep foundations.</p>\n<p>These procedures and timelines are set by the test methods and international standards that dictate all our procedures, from the size of the sample we use to the time each sample spends being prepared and processed.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2216,
                    "udi": "umb://media/698cf337e94d4322baf849089b18e828",
                    "image": "/media/ghzjy0kn/banner-2-min.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "<p> </p>\n<p>Our adherence to these international testing standards is how we maintain our accreditations and maintain an objective standard of quality assurance.</p>\n<p>The materials testing laboratory is often seen as something that just has to be checked off the list, but the work we do ensures the success of our client’s projects and the safety of their clients and the public.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>How can that misunderstanding impact the client’s expectations or experience?</strong></p>\n<p>It often leads to a client being disappointed or aggravated, as they are generally under pressure themselves to reach completion on their projects. This is why I constantly work to educate our clients on everything we do.</p>\n<p>We don’t expect them to be experts, that’s our job. But we want to provide a service they understand and trust.</p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        },
        {
          "name": "Article Split",
          "id": "d16b3e15-8507-43e3-b95b-836e0f7f1efa",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "6",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2208,
                    "udi": "umb://media/a8fd42b1020c472cb3efa2b51e4a9c5f",
                    "image": "/media/w3bp1kam/vlcsnap-2022-08-03-12h25m04s177-3-min.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2209,
                    "udi": "umb://media/eff851eb6bfb4efe9d751734a8c47996",
                    "image": "/media/3vipr151/vlcsnap-2022-08-03-12h25m04s177-3-min.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 2196,
                    "udi": "umb://media/be3ee2cb5bbd41b78e1eb42d22d0f932",
                    "image": "/media/zxrd3pv3/otms-5.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            },
            {
              "grid": "6",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p><strong>What excites you when you look at the construction industry in 2022 and beyond?</strong></p>\n<p>I am very excited about what is happening in the renewable energy sector. I believe we are going to receive a lot of work from those industries and that it will bring a long a lot of exciting new challenges.</p>\n<p>Second to that, it finally looks like our national routes in Gauteng are finally receiving some much needed attention, which is vital to maintain our infrastructure in the province.</p>\n<p>I feel that our industry was hit extremely hard by the pandemic. We lost a lot of construction companies that couldn't survive it.</p>\n<p>I am hoping that now that we have returned to some sort of normality, new opportunities will arise for those who have been down on their luck and that our industry can pick up some pace.</p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        },
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "dc43bb54-0a9c-484d-9cdd-ab0be06d0990",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span class=\"main-heading h1\">Interested in our work? Reach out to us below!</span></p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": null
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}]]></Value>
    </grid>
    <heroContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[<p>Our 7 accredited branches in Gauteng and the Western Cape, Eastern Cape and Free State are now joined by an accredited site laboratory, a first for Roadlab.</p>]]></Value>
    </heroContent>
